    "selected_package_instance_routes": 20,
    "qualification": "Each own manual supplies paired finite full-duplex master byte DMA: WIDTH7, both SIZE0, fixed DR endpoints, incrementing SRAM arrays, hardware BLOCK, REPEAT1 and paired clean terminal/request-close/BUSY-idle sequence. Own selectors are SPI1 RX/TX6/7 and F020/L052 SPI2 RX/TX8/9. No UART analogy or shared-IP-only admission is used.",
    "registers_and_irqs": "Seven own SPI instances, DR+0x18, CR1 DMARX16/DMATX17, SPI vectors25/26. F020 has native CH1/CH2 IRQ9/10; four-channel families have CH1/CH2+3/CH4 IRQ9/10/11. Full ISR/IER and typed R1W0 ICR/no-op0xff fields match own SVD/manual/current IR/PAC.",
    "semantic_limits": "DR read clears RXNE; MODF forces EN off and OV overwrites unread DR. Own TC/noTE/STATUS5 terminal proof does not turn EN-clear, gate closure, reset, timeout or BUSY0 after error into memory-drain evidence. BUSY supplies no clear interrupt or finite-liveness promise.",
